# IPC Debugger — Walkthrough

## What Was Built

A complete **IPC (Inter-Process Communication) Debugger** — a web-based tool for visualizing and debugging communication between processes, featuring:

- **Process Simulator** — processes with states (ready, running, waiting, blocked, terminated)
- **4 IPC Mechanisms** — Pipes, Message Queues, Shared Memory, Semaphores
- **Debugging Engine** — deadlock detection (cycle detection in wait-for graphs), race condition detection, bottleneck analysis
- **6 Built-in Scenarios** — Pipe Communication, Message Queue, Deadlock, Race Condition, Bottleneck, Complex Multi-IPC
- **Real-time Visualization** — animated SVG process graph with data flow particles
- **Timeline View** — color-coded process state history
- **Event Log** — timestamped log of all IPC events
- **Export Report** — downloadable debug report

